---
/*
 * The prints / buyer-reassurance section.
 *
 * This exists for two reasons at once. It answers the questions that stop
 * people from checking out ("is this real paper? what does archival mean?
 * what size do I need?"), and those same questions are high-volume searches,
 * so the section ranks while it sells.
 *
 * TODO: every number and claim below needs to be confirmed with Jennifer
 * before launch. Do NOT ship guessed specs about paper, inks, or editions —
 * these are promises to buyers.
 */
---

<section id="prints" class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="eyebrow">Prints &amp; Editions</p>
    <h2>What you're actually getting.</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      A print should feel like a real object, not a poster. Here's exactly how
      Jennifer's are made, so there are no surprises when the tube arrives.
    </p>

    <div class="prints">
      <article class="print-card">
        <h3>Archival giclée</h3>
        <p>
          Each print is made with pigment inks on heavyweight cotton rag paper —
          the same process galleries use. Pigment doesn't fade the way standard
          ink does, so the yellows and oranges stay as bright in ten years as
          they are the day it ships.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="print-card">
        <h3>Signed &amp; numbered</h3>
        <p>
          Limited editions are signed by hand and numbered in the margin — 12 of
          50, and when the fiftieth sells, the edition closes for good. Open
          editions are signed but not numbered, and stay available.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="print-card">
        <h3>Choosing a size</h3>
        <p>
          Above a console or a bed, go wider than feels right — roughly
          two-thirds the width of the furniture. For a gallery wall or a kitchen
          nook, the smaller sizes hold up better next to other frames. Unsure?
          Send Jennifer a photo of the wall and she'll tell you.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="print-card">
        <h3>Originals</h3>
        <p>
          Originals are acrylic on canvas, painted by hand, and there is exactly
          one of each. They ship unframed so you can choose a frame that suits
          the room, packed flat or rolled depending on size.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .prints {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
  }

  .print-card {
    padding: 1.75rem;
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--lemon);
  }

  .print-card:nth-child(2n) { border-top-color: var(--orange); }
  .print-card:nth-child(3n) { border-top-color: var(--leaf-light); }

  .print-card h3 { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }

  .print-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
</style>
